   "title": "There O.K.",
   "date": "June 22, 2023",
   "country": "United States",
   "variant": "Size: 34W x 32L Color: Olive",
   "verified_purchase": true,
   "helpful_votes": 1,
   "body": "These were O.K..I mean, they are nice. I like Express clothing pants better because they feel like pants. Thick. Durable. Nice, stretchy. Comfortable. But these Chino pants fit as expected in my normal size. I ordered my normal size. These have a different type of feeling material that I'm not used to. Would I order again? No, because they are really not for me. The style, ok, the feel, no. Will I return my order? No, I'll keep this in my inventory and figure out when and where to wear it, IF I wear it. Do I recommend others to buy? If your style is chino, try it out. Worst case scenario, return them. Hassle, sure, but you know buying clothes like this online has that risk they don't come as you expect. You really won't know till you try it. I don't know what I was expecting when I got these, they are my first chino pants, but I just won't be making another order, if Chino pants are like this. If this is how Chino pants feel and fit, and Chino pants was my style, yeah maybe I'd order more. Obviously as you see, I rated this a 5/5 stars. It deserves it for the comfort and value of money. But just the comfort and value of money. Can't say how long they will last though. Doesn't seem that durable but they will/should last a bit depending on the frequency in you wearing these and washing them. Though just because of the quality of feel, I don't know how these would feel after being wash and dried..."
