   "country": "United States",
   "variant": "Size: 36W x 30L Color: Charcoal",
   "verified_purchase": true,
   "helpful_votes": 2,
   "body": "I was wearing Dickies skinny straights for a while. 36x32 but the crotch would end up ripping after about 3 months. I tried True Classic chinos, goodfellow, and Dixxon but they were either too baggy (Dixxon), no stretch (goodfellow), or so stretchy the seams ripped (True Classic). So far these have stretch where I can do a Dennis Reynolds leg spread while being a slim fit similar to the dickies. The charcoal I purchased is VERY dark. Almost black/chocolate in some lighting. I’m excited to see if it lightens a little as most of my previous dickies did but faded to be too light. This should still retain some of its dark color even if it does fade. The waist has stretch, legs have stretch, all while staying slim. So far I’m loving these pants. Note: after washing I did lose about 1.5” off the inseam because it shrank. Otherwise, the pants fit the same."
