   "date": "October 16, 2024",
   "country": "Canada",
   "variant": "Size: 40W x 32L Color: Navy",
   "verified_purchase": true,
   "helpful_votes": 0,
   "body": "I wear a waist 38 x32 in just about all pants, which leaves me some room in the pants. With the differing opinions on the sizing for these Chino's, and being Asian made, I went a size up 40x32. They fit perfect. Just a little loose in the waist but I always wear a belt. So sizing is correct for myself at least, had I got my original size, these would have been simply tighter but not so much you look like a fruit (skintight on the calves). They are Cotton mostly, so allow if you put in the dryer, which I do not. They are not \"thick\" but they are not supposed to be, they are Chino's. Navy color is dark. Stitching on my pair is fine thus far, worn once, no washing. There is not much stretch fabric in them so I recommend getting your regular size. If you want them tight, go down your size. Want them a little loose, go a size up. These are not super skinny in the thighs, knee, calves and ankle, more regular slim fit ( at least for larger waist sizes ).Came a day early so that's a bonus. Good looking pants and I recommend them."
